<p>Pakistan carried out air strikes in Afghanistan, hitting targets in Kabul and Kandahar province, according to Afghanistan’s Taliban-led government and other local officials. Afghan officials said the strikes hit residential areas and killed at least four civilians. A Pakistani security official said the operation targeted the Pakistani Taliban (TTP), as tensions and cross-border fighting between the neighbors stretch into a third week. The Taliban said Pakistan bombed an airline fuel depot near Kandahar airport used by private carrier Kam Air.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/60XoVGctl0gqEwkLmyLRoFDjm2KMyN4FQqBNuPA1DzvB2PcRMd1rdYiTG82Dfk7zV9XuYIbnem-sI7R-83WjoWV_l30Le0DAadNtrFC9g0N17O7uMmaxiaeomB7l4gYOwJ5Rg2Kb55vBk3TTbu5VmTUSESYjtD01EYJGG3F6_Q' alt='Image accompanying reports on Afghan accusations that Pakistani airstrikes hit homes in Kabul and Kandahar.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Timing and spread: DW said Taliban officials described overnight Pakistani air force strikes in Kabul, as well as in several Afghan border provinces.</li><li>No immediate Pakistani comment: The Hindu said Pakistan’s military did not respond to a request for comment on the alleged strike near Kandahar airport.</li><li>Conflict scale: Reuters, via Al-Monitor, called this a major escalation in the worst fighting in years along the roughly 2,600 km border.</li><li>Reported lull before escalation: Al-Monitor said neither side reported Pakistani air strikes for more than a week, and ground clashes had eased before the Kandahar bombing.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Afghanistan’s Taliban government: Taliban officials accused Pakistan of striking residential homes in Kabul and Kandahar province. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/13/afghanistan-accuses-pakistan-of-air-attacks-on-homes-in-kabul-kandahar'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Pakistani security official: A Pakistani security official said the strikes targeted the Pakistani Taliban militant group (TTP). (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/pakistan-launches-fresh-strikes-on-kabul-and-border-provinces-afghan-govt-says'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>China (mediator): China has stepped up mediation between Pakistan and Afghanistan amid the latest clashes. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/pakistan-bombs-airline-fuel-depot-near-kandahar-airport-afghan-taliban-says'>Al-Monitor (via Reuters)</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/pakistan-launches-fresh-strikes-on-kabul-and-border-provinces-afghan-govt-says'>Pakistan launches fresh strikes on Kabul and border provinces, Afghan govt says</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-bombs-kabul-and-afghan-border-provinces/a-76341327'>Pakistan bombs Kabul and Afghan border provinces</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/pakistan-bombs-airline-fuel-depot-near-kandahar-airport-afghan-taliban/article70738161.ece'>Pakistan bombs airline fuel depot near Kandahar airport: Afghan Taliban</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/afghanistan-accuses-pakistan-targeting-homes-airstrikes-kill-4-131028580'>Afghanistan accuses Pakistan of targeting homes in airstrikes that kill at least 4 civilians</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/pakistan-strikes-kabul-killing-4-as-tensions-with-afghanistan-escalate-13988964.html'>Pakistan strikes Kabul, killing 4 as tensions with Afghanistan escalate</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/pakistan-bombs-airline-fuel-depot-near-kandahar-airport-afghan-taliban-says'>Pakistan bombs airline fuel depot near Kandahar airport, Afghan Taliban says</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/13/afghanistan-accuses-pakistan-of-air-attacks-on-homes-in-kabul-kandahar'>Afghanistan accuses Pakistan of air attacks on homes in Kabul, Kandahar</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>